//
// ScheduleService is the network surface over the scheduler: a durable registry
// of named schedules (cron / one-shot) that fire an agent run on a configured
// provider+model. It is a peer of HarnessService — the same package
// (`mecatl.v1`), the same wire conventions (string-passthrough kinds, no enum
// for the scheduler lifecycle), and the same `buf.validate.field` annotation
// posture (authored for documentation + future runtime enforcement; v1 enforces
// the required-field checks in the Go server adapter, see
// internal/adapter/server).
//
// The value objects mirror engine/port/schedule.go (ScheduleSpec /
// ScheduleState / Schedule / ScheduleFire / TriggerSpec /
// ScheduleProviderSelector / MisfirePolicy) one-for-one. The at-most-once
// claim-before-fire / singleton / pending-sentinel contract lives in the port
// doc-comments; this proto is a byte-faithful wire projection of it, never an
// reinterpretation.
//
// The schedule.* events (EvScheduleFired / EvScheduleSkipped / EvScheduleFailed)
// are emitted from COMPOSITION (the scheduler), NOT the agent loop, and ride the
// Event.schedule field (field 15) defined in harness.proto. For v1 they are
// DURABLE-LOG-ONLY: fired/failed events land in the fire session's EventLog
// (pull-only via GetFire/ListFires); skipped fires (no session) are
// operator-diag-only. A live broadcast stream is a future phase (ADR 0059
// decision #8, "pull-only delivery v1"). Their kind / stop / err are STRING
// passthroughs (the EvNoProgress / StopBudget discipline — no proto enum).

